                                                "sense_id": "e35d5291-0c45-3b71-a5ed-528ba86866ea",
                                                "text": "Hydrochloric acid is secreted by the parietal cells of the gastric glands, located on the wall of the fundus of the stomach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7de4434-26f0-49ab-a0b3-303336601c74",
                                                "sense_id": "e35d5291-0c45-3b71-a5ed-528ba86866ea",
                                                "text": "The superior aspect of the supramarginal gyrus lies underneath the euryon, which corresponds to the most prominent point of the parietal tuberosity or bossa […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe0b9dcb-35f5-3e9f-9423-fc45e7c591b5",
